{
 "info": {
  "name": "Spotter Fuel Route API",
  "description": "A truck trip inside the USA: the route, the cheapest places to buy fuel and the total cost. Start the server with `python manage.py runserver` and send request 1 first. It makes one request to OSRM, the free routing service; send it again and it makes none (`meta.external_api_calls`). Requests 2, 3, 4 and 12 change the truck or ask for more detail on the same trip, so they make none either. Requests 5 and 6 are new trips. Requests 7 to 11 show the errors. The demo video uses requests 1, 3 and 7.",
  "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
 },
 "variable": [
  {
   "key": "baseUrl",
   "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000"
  }
 ],
 "item": [
  {
   "name": "1. New York, NY → Los Angeles, CA",
   "request": {
    "method": "GET",
    "url": {
     "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/route?start=New York, NY&finish=Los Angeles, CA&start_tank=empty",
     "host": [
      "{{baseUrl}}"
     ],
     "path": [
      "api",
      "route"
     ],
     "query": [
      {
       "key": "start",
       "value": "New York, NY"
      },
      {
       "key": "finish",
       "value": "Los Angeles, CA"
      },
      {
       "key": "start_tank",
       "value": "empty",
       "description": "empty (default) = pay for every mile; full = leave with a free full tank"
      }
     ]
    },
    "description": "A long trip, about 2,800 miles, so the truck stops several times. Look at `fuel_stops` (each `decision.rule` says which of the three rules chose the stop), `summary.total_fuel_cost`, `summary.comparison` (a driver who ignores prices, for scale) and `meta.external_api_calls`: 1 the first time (the road comes from OSRM), 0 when you send it again. Copy `map.map_url` and open it in a browser to see the same plan on the guided page."
   },
   "event": [
    {
     "listen": "test",
     "script": {
      "type": "text/javascript",
      "exec": [
       "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
       "const body = pm.response.json();",
       "pm.test('has fuel stops and a total cost', () => {",
       "  pm.expect(body.fuel_stops.length).to.be.above(0);",
       "  pm.expect(body.summary.total_fuel_cost).to.be.above(0);",
       "});",
       "pm.test('every stop says which rule chose it', () => {",
       "  body.fuel_stops.forEach((s) => pm.expect(['reach_cheaper', 'finish', 'fill_up']).to.include(s.decision.rule));",
       "});",
       "pm.test('at most one request to OSRM (0 when sent again)', () => pm.expect(body.meta.external_api_calls).to.be.at.most(1));",
       "pm.test('the stop costs add up to the total, to the cent', () => {",
       "  const cents = body.fuel_stops.reduce((sum, s) => sum + Math.round(s.cost * 100), 0);",
       "  pm.expect(cents).to.eql(Math.round(body.summary.total_fuel_cost * 100));",
       "});",
       "console.log('stops', body.summary.number_of_stops, '| cost $' + body.summary.total_fuel_cost,",
       "  '| gallons', body.summary.total_gallons_purchased, '| calls to OSRM', body.meta.external_api_calls,",
       "  '| time', pm.response.headers.get('X-Response-Time-ms') + ' ms');",
       "console.log('map:', body.map.map_url);"
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "2. Truck: skip tiny stops (consolidate=true), 0 calls",
   "request": {
    "method": "GET",
    "url": {
     "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/route?start=New York, NY&finish=Los Angeles, CA&consolidate=true",
     "host": [
      "{{baseUrl}}"
     ],
     "path": [
      "api",
      "route"
     ],
     "query": [
      {
       "key": "start",
       "value": "New York, NY"
      },
      {
       "key": "finish",
       "value": "Los Angeles, CA"
      },
      {
       "key": "consolidate",
       "value": "true",
       "description": "false (default): the three rules alone, the cheapest plan. true: a stop that buys less than 10 gal is merged into a neighbour when that costs at most $1 more."
      }
     ]
    },
    "description": "The trip of request 1, with fewer, bigger stops: each tiny stop is merged into a nearby one if that costs at most a dollar more. Compare `summary.number_of_stops` and `summary.total_fuel_cost` with request 1; `summary.tiny_stops_merged` says how many stops the three rules alone make and what merging costs. Only the plan changes, not the road: no request to OSRM."
   },
   "event": [
    {
     "listen": "test",
     "script": {
      "type": "text/javascript",
      "exec": [
       "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
       "const body = pm.response.json();",
       "pm.test('no request to OSRM: the road of request 1 is reused', () => {",
       "  pm.expect(body.meta.external_api_calls).to.eql(0);",
       "  pm.expect(body.meta.route_cache).to.eql('hit');",
       "});",
       "pm.test('says what merging changed', () => {",
       "  pm.expect(body.summary.tiny_stops_merged.stops_before).to.be.at.least(body.summary.number_of_stops);",
       "  pm.expect(body.summary.tiny_stops_merged.extra_cost).to.be.at.least(0);",
       "});",
       "console.log('stops', body.summary.number_of_stops, '| cost $' + body.summary.total_fuel_cost,",
       "  '| gallons', body.summary.total_gallons_purchased, '| calls to OSRM', body.meta.external_api_calls,",
       "  '| time', pm.response.headers.get('X-Response-Time-ms') + ' ms');"
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
